// 247_weak_containers_removed.xr
// Expected: compile error — WeakMap and WeakSet no longer exist.
//
// Task 247 phase B removed them outright. They solved object-identity
// side-tables, not the problem RC actually needs a weak reference for
// (breaking a cycle); their clearing step is a finalizer in all but name,
// which spec 16.8 rejects; the two backends disagreed on what they meant
// (the VM released the key, AOT never did — so an AOT WeakMap was a strong
// map that only ever grew); and nothing in the repo used them.
//
// A deleted surface that still parses is worse than one that never existed,
// so this asserts both names are rejected rather than quietly accepted.

var wm = WeakMap<string, int>()
var ws = WeakSet<string>()
print(wm)
print(ws)
